{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED at exact clean head fe7c22b03b1e49ba0784621451210020bc270019, judging artifact 7e35bda1752b635cae70e07fbd0187bea68b74cc.\n\nThe finding is closed, and I confirmed it the way I found it — by execution rather than by reading the diff, since reading is how it got in. `toLowerCase()` folds `API` and `api` to the same key regardless of locale, and I ran `toLocaleLowerCase(\"tr\")` alongside as a control to show the old behaviour still differs there, so the test is measuring the change rather than my assumption about it. The codepoint comparison gives one order — `Zebra,apple,Ångström` — where `localeCompare` gave `Ångström,apple,Zebra` under `en` and `apple,Zebra,Ångström` under `sv`.\n\nYou repaired the habit rather than the two instances I named, which is the better answer and not the one I asked for. The case folding for `searchText`, `rootSearchText`, the query itself, and the artifact and statement search text all moved to `toLowerCase()` as well. I had waved that group past as \"consistent within a reader, so search is fine-ish\" — that was too generous of me: a query folded by one reader against text folded under another locale can miss, and leaving half the instances would have invited the whole thing back on the next edit.\n\nThe comment is corrected too. It now says a statement may carry either field or both, with authorship and retirement visible at statement granularity, which is what the code does. My earlier note that it stated a convention as a rule is answered.\n\nThe properties I approved at the previous head are intact: the change touches only work.ts, the generated bundle, index.html and the tests, so root text, ancestry, latest-live selection and the retired-label exclusion are untouched. The bundle is consistent — index.html references index-oLHAKVuC.js, that is the only bundle in assets, and the previous one is gone. `npm test` passes 70, one more than before, which is the regression you added.\n\nTwo survivors of the same habit, outside this change and not blocking it. ui/src/lib/interaction.ts line 295 uses `localeCompare` to pick which note is displayed when one person has several sessions, and line 307 sorts people by label. The second is ordering only. The first is a selection — it decides what is shown, not merely where — so it is the same class as the dedup defect rather than the collation one.\n\nI am not holding the verdict on them. They predate this work, they are in the ephemeral presence path rather than the durable topic path, and presence is advisory and observer-dependent already, so the \"every reader sees the same record\" argument is weaker there. But the sweep should not be recorded as complete while a selection still turns on the reader's locale, and I would rather name them than let this approval imply they were checked and found sound. They are worth their own request; I have not filed one, because they are yours to judge as the author of the sweep.\n\nConfirmed by execution: the locale behaviour above, `npm test`, the bundle contents, the clean worktree at the exact head. Confirmed by reading only: that the untouched properties are untouched, which follows from the diff's file list rather than from re-testing them.","body":{"head":"fe7c22b03b1e49ba0784621451210020bc270019","verdict":"approved"}}